{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nsrcs=d.get('sources',[])\nfor s in [{\\\"id\\\":\\\"snapshot_trigger\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replication.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":222,\\\"end_line\\\":224,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n          {\\\"id\\\":\\\"user_restore_hole\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1097,\\\"end_line\\\":1199,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}]:\n    if not any(x['id']==s['id'] for x in srcs): srcs.append(s)\nd['sources']=srcs\nbase_statement=(\\\"A configuration that a node holds only in its log can be restored to that node's in-memory state by four paths, of which only one is in-protocol: a later configuration entry \\\"\n \\\"replicated by a correctly configured leader (appendEntries processes new configuration entries); an operator restart with RestoreCommittedLogs disabled; RecoverCluster on the stopped node with the \\\"\n \\\"configuration supplied, which writes a snapshot carrying it and truncates the log so the next NewRaft restores it from the snapshot; and an installed snapshot, whose metadata carries the configuration. \\\"\n \\\"In the restart scenarios recorded here none of the four is triggered by the node's own restart: a leader sends a snapshot only to a follower that lacks already-compacted entries (replication.go 222-224), \\\"\n \\\"and the affected node's log is complete, so no snapshot is sent to it and no configuration entry reaches it uncommitted. The snapshot path is nevertheless reachable for a node with a complete log whenever \\\"\n \\\"the leader's own log has a hole above that node's next index, as after a leader-side user restore, which deliberately leaves such a hole (raft.go 1097-1199); and where every voter restarts with the flag \\\"\n \\\"enabled and no covering snapshot, the in-protocol path needs a leader that the empty configuration prevents from being elected, so the cluster stays unavailable until an operator acts.\\\")\nd['knowledge']=[{\n \\\"id\\\":\\\"6420ecc11ae840028bf3e70220f5fd17-knowledge-1\\\",\n \\\"kind\\\":\\\"fact\\\",\n \\\"statement\\\":base_statement,\n \\\"conditions\\\":d['knowledge'][0]['conditions'],\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"append_new_entries\\\",\\\"snapshot_install_config\\\",\\\"bootstrap_refusal\\\",\\\"recover_cluster\\\",\\\"snapshot_trigger\\\",\\\"user_restore_hole\\\"],\n \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"6d6abaf163524e64878c6c9810de2461\\\":[5],\\\"4f4a771f03b649c2a5703b0ff279ff3a\\\":[1],\\\"0440f054115e44f4a0234c7a4ef67150\\\":[1,2],\\\"81163da076c64417bd48e0f79260d73d\\\":[2]},\n \\\"changed_premise\\\":(\\\"Correction narrowing an over-broad claim: the previous revision said that no repair path works on a running node with a complete log, but the snapshot path can reach such a node when the leader's own log has a hole above the node's next index, \\\"\n  \\\"which a leader-side user restore deliberately creates; the trigger for sending a snapshot on a missing previous entry is replication.go 222-224 and the hole is created by the restore path in raft.go 1097-1199. The statement now scopes the 'no path is triggered by the node's own restart' claim to the restart scenarios observed here and states the exception explicitly. \\\"\n  \\\"Conditions, the other three paths, all executions and the earlier evidence are unchanged.\\\")\n}]\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations']=[l.replace(\\\"so no snapshot is ever sent to it in these scenarios.\\\",\\\"so no snapshot is sent to it in these scenarios (with the caveat, found while re-reading the snapshot path, that a leader-side user restore leaves a hole above such a node's next index and does send it one, replication.go 222-224 with raft.go 1097-1199).\\\") for l in par['limitations']]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nPYEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
